    "citation": "Spektrafilm by Andrea Volpato and contributors; https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm . New calibration, not an upstream stock profile.",
    "datasource": "Kodak Ektachrome 64 Professional Film (EPR), publication E-8; SHA256 d9e046d5307c847aef2bebbcc067defdc3280c4876c07567f284ed8f231814a1. Reproduce with scripts/bw_expansion/prepare_colour_film.py; axis calibration derived from the page by scripts/bw_expansion/extract_graphs.py; source points, assumptions and conditions: data/profile-sources/kodak-ektachrome64-epr/recipe.json. Dye spectra: this sheet, rescaled against its own visual neutral. PCHIP of the three plotted log-sensitivity traces; engine covers 380-780 nm, each trace is used only over its own plotted span and is unmeasured elsewhere. Relative shape only; the panel's E.N.D. density criterion is not an absolute speed. Not on the sheet. The dye panel is normalised to a visual neutral of 1.0 and plots no D-min, and the characteristic panel's minimum is a status-A reading, not a spectral curve. A flat 0.10 is assumed, within the 0.09-0.13 range the shipped positives carry. This is an assumption, not a measurement. Spectral adaptation parameters are not this stock's own: they are borrowed from kodak_ektachrome_100. Nearest shipped sibling: the same manufacturer's E-6 reversal film. Donor choice is worth about 7 chroma points - borrowing from Ektachrome 100 renders at 72.3 against the shipped profile's 71.1, Kodachrome 64 at 75.0, Provia 100F at 77.1, Velvia 100 at 78.2, and Portra 400, a negative, at 79.6. Every donor beats having none, which is 88.0. Density curves balanced against a rendered 5-stop grey ramp by scripts/bw_expansion/balance_against_ramp.py (upstream's correct_positive_curves_with_gray_ramp): density scale [0.9826, 0.9777, 1.0433], log-exposure shift [-0.0562, 0.0, 0.0245], data_trustability 0.5. Worst channel deviation from neutral across the ramp 38.0% before, 2.6% after. This correction is fitted against the engine, not measured from the datasheet."
  },
